      "message": "Since the only bit changing is the DP connection bit, I\u0027d suggest something like: \n\nint bb_retimer_set_dp_connection(struct usb_mux *me, bool enable)\n\nThat API could be used by both the HPD update and mux set interfaces.  The logic for how/when to change the bit should be in the board code.\n\nSo for example, the board\u0027s hpd update would have:\n``` \nbb_retimer_hpd_update()\n\nif (hpd_state \u0026 USB_PD_MUX_HPD_LVL)\n    bb_retimer_set_dp_connection(me, true)\nelse if (framework check)\n    bb_retimer_set_dp_connection(me, false)\n```\n\nThe board\u0027s mux set would have: \n```\nif (framework check) \n    bb_retimer_set_dp_connection(me, false)\n```\n\nYou could also choose to structure with a guard clause, such that both functions call `if(!framework) return` once you get to the card specific behaviors, ex. \n```\nbb_retimer_hpd_update()\n\nif (!framework)\n   return;\n   \nif (hpd_state \u0026 USB_PD_MUX_HPD_LVL)\n    bb_retimer_set_dp_connection(me, true)\nelse\n    bb_retimer_set_dp_connection(me, false)\n```",
